  "a2-s4a04-ssh-amd64-1/2": "amd64 target build failed (exec format error): the earlier privileged Ubuntu target ran systemd-binfmt, which cleared the Docker VM Rosetta binfmt registration; restored and masked (see incident)"
 },
 "incident": "Between about 12:55 and 13:10 UTC the privileged arm64 target ran systemd-binfmt (and likely systemd-sysctl) against the shared Docker Desktop VM kernel, unregistering Rosetta amd64 emulation for every lane and registering python3.10. The Rosetta entry was re-registered with its standard magic/mask and POCF flags and the python3.10 entry removed; amd64 containers run again. Ubuntu sysctl hardening values may have been applied VM-wide (printk 4 4 1 7, sysrq 176, kptr_restrict 1, pid_max 4194304); their prior values are unknown and were not changed back; a Docker Desktop restart resets them. The fixture now masks these units and the runner asserts binfmt/sysctl state is unchanged before and after each target.",
 "commands": [
  "cargo test -p oo-stack -p oo-cli --locked",
  "python3 -m unittest discover -s deploy/lite -p test_*.py",
  "python3 deploy/lite/build_images.py --run-id <id> --platforms linux/amd64",
  "cargo build -p oo-cli --locked",
  "python3 deploy/lite/test_remote_ssh.py --run-id <id> --arch arm64 --offline --password-case --image-arm64 <arm64 digest> --image-amd64 <amd64 digest>",
  "python3 deploy/lite/test_remote_ssh.py --run-id <id> --arch amd64 --image-arm64 <arm64 digest> --image-amd64 <amd64 digest>"
 ],
